<h2>Overview</h2>
<p>Meridian's online scheduler made patients call the office more often than it saved them a call. I led the redesign of the booking flow, cutting completion time roughly in half and dropping scheduling-related support calls by a third.</p>

<h2>Problem</h2>
<p>Patients abandoned the flow at the "choose a time" step. The calendar showed every slot for every provider at once, with no way to filter by location or insurance, so people gave up and phoned the front desk — the exact outcome the tool was meant to prevent.</p>

<h2>Goals &amp; constraints</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Goal:</strong> reduce booking-flow abandonment and scheduling support calls.</li>
  <li><strong>Constraint:</strong> the underlying EHR API couldn't change; we designed around its existing slot data.</li>
  <li><strong>Constraint:</strong> launch had to meet WCAG AA — it's a healthcare product.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Research</h2>
<p>Five booking sessions made the core insight obvious: people think in terms of <em>"the soonest appointment near me,"</em> not <em>"provider, then date, then time."</em> The flow was organized backwards from how patients reasoned about it.</p>

<figure class="cs-figure">
  <img src="/assets/examples/example-process.svg" alt="Research-to-test loop: research, sketch, wireframe, test, repeat">
  <figcaption>The loop the team ran each sprint.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>Process &amp; design decisions</h2>
<p>We inverted the flow to lead with location and "soonest available," and deferred provider selection to the end for the patients who cared about it. A reusable date-and-time component replaced the wall-of-slots calendar.</p>

<figure class="cs-figure">
  <img src="/assets/examples/example-wireframe.svg" alt="Annotated wireframe of the reordered booking flow with three numbered callouts">
  <figcaption>Callouts: (1) lead with location filter, (2) surface the soonest slot, (3) defer provider choice — the reordering that fixed the drop-off.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>Final solution</h2>
<p>The shipped experience: a filter-first flow with the soonest appointment surfaced up top, and a confirmation step that sets a reminder in one tap.</p>

